    "# Safe deep reinforcement learning for dynamic separator control with NeqSim\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook couples a high-fidelity NeqSim dynamic separator with a Deep Q-Network (DQN).\n",
    "The controller coordinates the feed, gas-outlet, and liquid-outlet valves while tracking liquid\n",
    "level and separator pressure. A conventional proportional-integral (PI) controller provides an\n",
    "engineering benchmark.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Learning objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "After completing the notebook, you can:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. build a transient separator, valves, transmitters, and process system with current NeqSim APIs;\n",
    "2. expose a process simulator through a reinforcement-learning state, action, and reward interface;\n",
    "3. train a DQN efficiently with replay memory, a target network, and expert-guided initialization;\n",
    "4. apply a safety supervisor before an action reaches the process;\n",
    "5. test nominal control, scheduled setpoint changes, and a reusable custom scenario;\n",
    "6. compare the learned policy with native NeqSim PI control; and\n",
    "7. save and reload the trained controller with a numerical identity check.\n",
    "\n",
    "The synthetic fluid and operating conditions are educational. They are not a certified separator\n",
    "design or a production control policy. The related\n",
    "[dynamic separator example](https://github.com/EvenSol/NeqSim-Colab/blob/master/notebooks/process/dynsep.ipynb)\n",
    "uses the same type of transient equipment."
   ]
  },
