    "## 2. Control formulation and NeqSim environment\n",
    "\n",
    "The measured state contains liquid level $L$, separator pressure $P$, feed rate $\\dot{m}$,\n",
    "tracking errors, and the three valve openings. Each valve can close, hold, or open by two\n",
    "percentage points. Their Cartesian product gives 27 simultaneous actions.\n",
    "\n",
    "The normalized state is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{x} =\n",
    "\\left[\n",
    "L,\\ \\frac{P}{10},\\ \\frac{\\dot{m}}{300},\\\n",
    "L-L_{sp},\\ \\frac{P-P_{sp}}{10},\\\n",
    "\\frac{u_f}{100},\\ \\frac{u_g}{100},\\ \\frac{u_l}{100}\n",
    "\\right].$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Here, $L_{sp}$ is the level setpoint, $P_{sp}$ is the pressure setpoint in bara, and\n",
    "$u_f$, $u_g$, and $u_l$ are valve openings in percent. The reward penalizes normalized tracking\n",
    "error and excessive movement:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$r_t =\n",
    "-4\\left(\\frac{L_t-L_{sp}}{0.10}\\right)^2\n",
    "-2\\left(\\frac{P_t-P_{sp}}{0.50}\\right)^2\n",
    "-0.02\\left\\|\\Delta\\mathbf{u}_t\\right\\|_1.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The environment calls NeqSim for every transition. The safety supervisor only constrains action\n",
    "direction when a measurement is already outside the stated control band; it does not replace the\n",
    "DQN or change the simulated process."
   ]
  },
